          "Validating synthetic capacity limits locally via `VRAMBudgetGuard` before touching GPU queues builds strong reproducibility across heterogeneous cluster allocations. Moving a workload from an `80 GB` H100 (`72.0 GB` usable ceiling) onto an older `40 GB` A100 node simply updates `gpu_capacity_gb=40.0` (`36.0 GB` usable ceiling), raising immediate deterministic `MemoryError` guards (`OOM_PREVENTED`) whenever `40.0 + 15.0 = 55.0 GB` spills past physical card capabilities.",
