          "Comparing baseline Data Parallelism against DeepSpeed ZeRO via `ZERO_STAGES_TAXONOMY` highlights where standard DDP wastes gigabytes of high-bandwidth memory. In naive DDP, every GPU holds identical replicas of all 16 static bytes per weight: 2B parameters, 2B gradients, and 12B FP32 AdamW buffers (`master + momentum + variance`). On an 8-GPU node running a 13B model, eight replicas store the exact same optimizer states simultaneously, burning eight times more total HBM than mathematically needed just so each replica updates weights independently after gradient All-Reduce.",
