          "Contrasting `ZERO_STAGES_TAXONOMY` highlights how Microsoft DeepSpeed’s Zero Redundancy Optimizer (`ZeRO`) methodically erases wasteful duplicate state across Data Parallel ranks (`N` GPUs) without shrinking global mathematical batch fidelity. Standard DDP clones parameters (`2B`), gradients (`2B`), and FP32 AdamW buffers (`12B`) across all `N` GPUs (`16N` total cluster bytes for identical optimizer updates!). Stepping cleanly through `ZERO_STAGE_1` (shard `12B` optimizer states -> `4x` static savings), `ZERO_STAGE_2` (also shard `2B` gradients -> `8x`), and `ZERO_STAGE_3` (shard live `2B` weights too -> full `N`-way compression) systematically conquers cluster VRAM walls.",
