          "Evaluating the exact byte-per-parameter formulas inside `ZeROStageMemoryCalculator.calculate_memory_per_gpu_gb` reveals how sharply each stage compresses per-GPU static memory. Setting `p = param_billions * 1e9`, unsharded DDP (`stage=0`) retains `16.0 * p` bytes (`2B weights + 2B grads + 12B Adam`). `'ZeRO-1'` keeps 2B weights and 2B grads replicated (`4.0 * p`) while dividing 12B optimizer states by `num_gpus`: `(4.0 * p) + (12.0 * p / num_gpus)`. `'ZeRO-2'` shards gradients too (`2.0 * p + 14.0 * p / num_gpus`), and `'ZeRO-3'` shards every tensor equally (`16.0 * p / num_gpus`) before dividing by `1024**3`.",
