          "One practical detail when toggling Sequence Parallelism on `TP=8` runs involves Dropout random number generator (RNG) state alignment! Outside TP blocks, independent sequence shards hold different tokens per rank, so each GPU can safely advance its own distinct local RNG seed for Dropout; inside Tensor Parallel attention/MLP layers, ranks must still synchronize shared TP RNG trackers so ColumnParallel dropout drops matching mask features across shards. Mixing those two RNG trackers produces subtle training convergence bugs if custom layers forget which zone is sequence-sharded versus tensor-sharded.",
