          "Ensuring sequence-local statistics remain accurate requires remembering why `LayerNorm` / `RMSNorm` scales across feature vector axis `hidden_dim` (which stays *completely un-sharded* inside SP!) rather than sequence axis `seq_len`. Every GPU owns full `4096` hidden features for its `[1024]` local sequence tokens, computing exact `LayerNorm`/`RMSNorm` zero-comm locally without touching neighbor GPUs!",
