          "Asymmetric kernel epilogue fusion underpins delayed scaling (`simulate_delayed_scaling`) zero-sync speedups on H100 GPUs. Recording current `abs_max` (`amax`) scalars straight inside hardware tensor registers as an output epilogue of Tensor Core `WGMMA` matrix multiplies costs practically zero extra HBM memory bandwidth—turning historical `amax_history` sweeps (`[12.4, 15.2, 14.8, 16.0] -> next_scale = 26.6`) into single arithmetic updates ready instantaneously for Step `t + 1`!",
