          "Handling activation spikes in attention heads requires coordinating delayed scaling with causal attention masking to prevent score explosion.",
          "Automated saturation monitors verify that format clipping occurs on less than one hundredth of a percent of all computed elements.",
          "Preventing overflow inversions inside delayed FP8 loops demands real-time clamping checks implemented in `validate_fp8_scaling_guardrail`. Before casting a raw tensor of observed maximum magnitude `tensor_amax` into E4M3 using previously computed `scale`, multiplying `scaled_max = tensor_amax * scale` checks directly whether the product breached `fp8_max` (`448.0`). Calling `(tensor_amax=18.5, scale=24.0, fp8_max=448.0)` evaluates `18.5 * 24.0 = 444.0 <= 448.0`, confirming strict headroom inside E4M3 range and returning `(\"FP8_SCALING_STABLE\", True)`.",
