          "Production Transformer Engine runtimes avoid silent `NaN` conversion by hardware-clamping scaled floats to `±448.0` (`torch.clamp(..., -448, 448)`) during FP8 conversion kernels, yet logging `FP8_E4M3_OVERFLOW_CLIPPING` events still matters immensely! Repeated clipping events (`> 0.1%` of steps) indicate overly stale `amax_history` windows (`e.g., amax_history_len` too long to decay down fast or too rigid against outlier bursts) or insufficient safety margins (`margin_bits`), signaling teams to shorten history lookback or tighten `fp8_max * 0.90`.",
