          "Routing entropy provides a sensitive mathematical metric for detecting early signs of expert collapse before loss curves diverge.",
          "Routing entropy is calculated as: -sum(f_i * log2(f_i)), measuring the statistical uniformity of token dispatch fractions across experts.",
          "For an 8-expert model, maximum entropy equals log2(8) = 3.0 bits, representing perfectly uniform token distribution across all experts.",
