          "If routing entropy drops precipitously following a learning rate warmup phase, the optimizer schedule can be paused and adjusted.",
          "Proactive entropy guardrails prevent multi-million-dollar training campaigns from collapsing into degraded representational states.",
          "Enforcing structural diversity checks ensures that all provisioned expert parameters actively participate in knowledge acquisition.",
          "Measuring router diversity holistically beyond single scalar means relies on Shannon Entropy (`-sum(f * math.log2(f))`) validated inside `validate_routing_entropy_guardrail`. Unlike simple max-drop checks (`D51`), Shannon Entropy simultaneously penalizes *dead experts* (experts receiving zero tokens contribute `0`) and monopolizing experts in one single bounded unit measured in bits (`[0, log2(num_experts)]`)! Across `num_experts=8`, maximum theoretical entropy equals `log2(8) = 3.0 bits`. Passing uniform `[0.125]*8` yields `entropy = 3.0 >= min_entropy (2.5)`, returning `(\"ROUTING_DISTRIBUTION_HEALTHY\", True)`.",
          "Walking through pathological failure distributions reveals why `validate_routing_entropy_guardrail` flags silent dead-expert waste missed by naive balance averages! Suppose `4` experts take `[0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25]` while Experts `4..7` sit completely untouched (`[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]`) at lower `capacity_factor`: Shannon entropy immediately drops from `3.0 bits` down to `log2(4) = 2.0 bits < 2.5`, immediately catching `'EXPERT_ENTROPY_COLLAPSE: Distribution collapsed'` (`4` wasted GPUs hosting dead dormant weights across the entire node cluster!).",
          "Notice that explicit positive filtering guard (`if f > 0`) avoids Python `math.log2(0)` ValueError exceptions cleanly inside online validation sweeps. Even when transient topic batches skew one expert momentarily to zero during tiny evaluation slices, summing `f * math.log2(f)` strictly over positive terms implements exact information-theoretic `0 * log(0) = 0` convention without crashing monitoring pipelines midway through evaluation runs.",
          "Logging entropy alongside `aux_loss` and token drop percentages gives cluster engineers complete spatial observability across every `EP` group—ensuring all `8` hardware expert shards pull useful compute evenly.",
          "Information-theoretic router diagnostics inside `validate_routing_entropy_guardrail` (`-sum(f * log2(f)) -> 3.0 >= 2.5` on `[0.125]*8`) detect subtle dead-expert starvation hidden behind benign scalar drop averages. Four overloaded experts absorbing uniform `0.25` slices while four sibling experts sit completely idle yield zero capacity drops cleanly at `cf=2.0`, yet leave half of cluster GPU silicon completely unused—a structural failure caught instantly once Shannon entropy plunges down to `2.0 bits < 2.5`!",
