          "Measuring exact adapter savings across adaptation regimes inside `calculate_peft_memory_footprint` proves why LoRA and QLoRA democratized 70B customization overnight. Evaluating a massive `70.0B` model with `rank=16`, `hidden_dim=8192`, `num_layers=80` calculates full mixed-precision AdamW memory (`16 * params_b`) at an astronomical `1120.0 GB`—requiring sixteen 80 GB GPUs minimum before activations! Freezing base weights in BF16 (`2 * 70 = 140 GB`) while training AdamW exclusively on tiny rank-16 Q/K/V/O projections (`adapter_params = 8 * 80 * 16 * 8192 = 83.89M` parameters, costing ~`1.3 GB` static trainer buffers!) plunges total footprint down eightfold to `LoRA = 141.3 GB`.",
