          "Examining exact byte savings breakdown highlights why frozen parameters shrink footprint *far more than 2x* when switching to PEFT! Under full fine-tuning, every billion parameters drags along `2 GB` gradients + `12 GB` FP32 AdamW buffers alongside `2 GB` weights (`14 GB` non-weight trainer overhead per billion params!). Freezing base matrices removes `100%` of those `14 GB` gradient and AdamW vectors across all `70.0B` base weights—requiring `16`-byte optimizer states strictly for just the `0.084B` trainable adapter parameters (`83.89M * 16 ~ 1.34 GB`)!",
