          "Quantization granularity choices explain how `calculate_peft_memory_footprint` shrinks `1120.0 GB` full AdamW down through `LoRA` (`141.3 GB`) straight into single-GPU `QLoRA` (`36.3 GB`, `Adapters: 83.89M params`). Blockwise `NF4` quantization groups weights into tiny `64`-element blocks matching Gaussian trained weight quantiles while double-quantizing blockwise scaling constants into FP8 (`saving 0.37 bits/param`), shrinking frozen 70B models ~`4x` smoothly without noticeable perplexity drop.",
          "Forward on-the-fly dequantization unpacks active 4-bit blocks transiently inside GPU SRAM registers solely during `W0 @ x` GEMMs before releasing unpacked BF16 tiles immediately, holding static memory cleanly under `40 GB`.",
