          "Note an important statistical subtlety when scaling `detect_cluster_stragglers` past `N = 8` up to `512` GPUs with extreme severe outliers (`e.g., Rank 4 takes 10.0s` instead of `1.85s`). Under severe single-rank distortion, sensitive sample `mean` and `stdev` expand wildly together—sometimes inflating `mean + 2*stdev` past moderate slowdowns (`masking phenomenon`)! Production cluster watchdogs therefore track *median + k * MAD* (Median Absolute Deviation) alongside sample `mean + 2 * stdev` so multi-second hangs never blind threshold statistics across large fleets.",
